        <mxCell id="wGQi0n4J2-Beg7k2Higl-11" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;State v. Shack&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- employs migrant works, houses, feeds and does everything for them.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- race, color, religion, origin, civil rights act&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="240" x="13410" y="23.13" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wGQi0n4J2-Beg7k2Higl-12" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Facts&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Tejeras and Southwest Citizens Organization for Poverty Elimination, known by the acronym SCOPE, a nonprofit corporation funded by the Office of&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Economic Opportunity pursuant to an act of Congress,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Defendant Shack is a staff attorney with the Farm Workers Division&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;of Camden Regional Legal Services, Inc., known as &quot;CRLS,&quot; also a&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;nonprofit corporation funded by the Office of Economic Opportunity&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;pursuant to an act of Congress, 42 U.S.C.A. § 2809(a)(3). The mission of CRLS includes legal advice and representation for these workers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Tedesco also offered to locate the man but insisted that the consultation would have to take place in Tedesco&#39;s office and in his presence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Defendants declined, saying they&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;had the right to see the men in the privacy of their living quarters and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;without Tedesco&#39;s [supervision].&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- A man&#39;s right in his real property of course is not absolute. It was a&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;maxim of the common law that one should so use his property as not to&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;injure the rights of others.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Necessity can&#39;t be used, becuse there isn&#39;t enough immediate harm to justify necessity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Property rights serve human values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Owns the land, but does not own the destiny of the people there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="452.5" width="400" x="13610" y="207.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wGQi0n4J2-Beg7k2Higl-13" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rules&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="240" x="13330" y="345" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wGQi0n4J2-Beg7k2Higl-14" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Issue&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="210" x="13170" y="195" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-1" edge="1" parent="1" source="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#00FF00);entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-7">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="14400" y="144" />
              <mxPoint x="14380" y="144" />
              <mxPoint x="14380" y="184" />
              <mxPoint x="14165" y="184" />
            </Array>
            <mxPoint x="14190" y="223.75" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#3399FF);" target="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-5">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-3" edge="1" parent="1" source="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#FF33FF);" target="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-6">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RUYWs7uuwX0-735RAe2n-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="RUYWs7uuwX0-735RAe2n-3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-4" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Uston v. Resorts International Hotel, Inc.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- pro card counter&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- take customers on a first come first serve basis on capacity &amp;nbsp;- not a who is most likely to spend/loose the most money basis&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- charging reasonable rate&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Inns and common carriers, not so dangerous anymore because there are other options&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="156.25" width="270" x="14280" y="-10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-5" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Facts&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Uston, our plaintiff, was a professional poker player and teacher, he was so good, becuse he had an amazing memory and counted cards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- January 5, 1979, however, a new Commission rule took effect&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;that dramatically improved the card counter&#39;s odds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- thus, &amp;nbsp;Resorts subsequently formulated standards for identification of card counters and adopted a general policy to exclude&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;such players. Killing Uston&#39;s&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;career at its blackjack tables.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- The Commission upheld Resorts&#39; decision to exclude Uston. Relying on Garifine v. Monmouth Park Jockey Club, 148 A.2d 1 (N.J. 1959), the Commission held that Resorts enjoys a common law right to exclude anyone it chooses, as long as the exclusion does not violate state and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;federal civil rights laws. (non discrimination)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;and being good at memorization is not a protected class&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- The casino control act has so many and very persist rules. So many that the court saw them as exhaustive statutes and regulations make clear that the&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Commission&#39;s control over the rules and conduct of licensed casino games&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;is intended to be comprehensive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- The Commission alone has the authority to exclude patrons based upon their strategies for playing licensed casino games.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Any common law right Resorts may have had to exclude Uston for these&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;reasons is abrogated by the act.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Despite the fact that it doesn&#39;t matter for this case, they wanted to address &lt;i&gt;absolute right to exclude patrons without good cause&lt;/i&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Mentions the&amp;nbsp;Fourteenth Amendment,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- &quot;the more private property is devoted to public use, the more it must accommodate the rights . . . of the general public who use that property.&quot;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- &lt;i&gt;Schmid&lt;/i&gt; recognizes implicitly that when property owners open their&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;premises to the general public in the pursuit of their own property&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;interests, they have no right to exclude people unreasonably.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;common carriers,( railroad)&amp;nbsp;innkeepers,&amp;nbsp;gasoline service stations, but to all property owners who open their premises&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;to the public. Property owners have no legitimate interest in unreasonably excluding particular members of the public when they open their premises for public use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- No party in this appeal questions the right of property owners to&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;exclude from their premises those whose actions &quot;disrupt the regular and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;essential operations of the [premises],&quot;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-no Commission rule banning Uston,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Illinois law, held that a horse racing park could&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;exclude a group of &quot;self-proclaimed expert handicappers&quot; from the park for&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;any reason or no reason at all, as long as there was no discrimination based&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;on &quot;race, color, creed, national origin, or sex.&quot;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;policy matter, my honest thoughts: I agree with this ruling more. With the predictive power we have today for consumers it would be ridiculous if a company only allow high risk buyers into their store and business&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1446.25" width="250" x="14460" y="223.75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-6" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rules&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- The common law right to exclude is substantially limited by a competing&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;common law right of &lt;b&gt;reasonable access to public places.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="240" x="14190" y="373.75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-7" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Issue&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) does a casino have the right to exclude beyond discrimination&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="210" x="14060" y="217.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-8" edge="1" parent="1" source="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-11" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#00FF00);">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="15120" y="148.75" />
              <mxPoint x="15120" y="188.75" />
              <mxPoint x="14930" y="188.75" />
            </Array>
            <mxPoint x="14930" y="228.75" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-9" edge="1" parent="1" source="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-11" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#3399FF);" target="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-12">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-10" edge="1" parent="1" source="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-11" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#FF33FF);" target="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-13">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-11" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Shelley v. Kraemer&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Can people discriminate privately in HOAs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="240" x="15020" y="61.25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-12" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Facts&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Kraemer were a black family who had just moved into a white nehiborhood&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- where they signed an agreement basically saying this was a white only nehiborhood&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Shelley then sued for the property to be taken from then, as per the agreement they as a black family were not allowed to own the property &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Whether the equal protection clause of the Fourteenth Amendment&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;inhibits judicial enforcement by state courts of restrictive covenants&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;based on race or color is a question which this Court has not heretofore&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;been called upon to consider.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Lists several state and city ordinances that where discriminatory&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- this case distinguishes by being about private citizen vs. private citizen&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- We conclude, therefore, that the restrictive agreements standing&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;alone cannot be regarded as a violation of any rights guaranteed to&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;petitioners by the Fourteenth Amendment. So long as the purposes of&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;those agreements are effectuated by voluntary adherence to their terms, becuse the state was not involved&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- The undisputed facts disclose&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;that petitioners were willing purchasers of properties upon which they&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;desired to establish homes. The owners of the properties were willing&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;sellers; and contracts of sale were accordingly consummated. - this is not voluntary, if it was, that would be legal, but what she is asking for is state intervention&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- We have noted that freedom from discrimination by the&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;States in the enjoyment of property rights was among the basic objectives&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;sought to be effectuated by the framers of the Fourteenth Amendment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- any resulting judicial&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;judgment is state action, and hence is subject to the limitations of the&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Constitution, including the Equal Protection Clause.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="851.25" width="250" x="15200" y="228.75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-13" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rules&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="240" x="14930" y="378.75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="irL610NNTSOzzAm699FG-14" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Issue&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1)&amp;nbsp;Can people discriminate privately in HOAs rules&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="210" x="14770" y="228.75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RUYWs7uuwX0-735RAe2n-1" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="Traditional common law - inn and common carriers&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Civil rights act -&amp;nbsp;race, color, religion, origin, not common carriers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="240" x="13780" y="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RUYWs7uuwX0-735RAe2n-3" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="Traditional common law vs. Uston newer one - all busineses are public&amp;nbsp;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="111.88" width="175" x="14705" y="38.13" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Claude question&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;True or false: In Jacque v. Steenberg Homes, Inc., the court held that a landowner who suffers an intentional trespass may be awarded punitive damages only if they can also prove actual, compensable harm — such as physical damage to the property or economic loss. Briefly explain.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="300" x="240" y="-190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-6" edge="1" parent="1" source="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-5" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;my answer&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;nominal damages can support punitive damages because society values the right to exclude, and only awarding nominal damages would not disincentives trespass enough.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="300" x="340" y="-410" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-8" edge="1" parent="1" source="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-7" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-5" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Claude rewrites&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;nominal damages can support punitive damages for &lt;b&gt;intentional trespass&lt;/b&gt; because society values the right to exclude regardless of physical or economic harm only awarding nominal damages would incentivize &lt;b&gt;&quot;self-help&quot; building walls, guns, to keep others out, and society wants to avoid that. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="300" x="380" y="-630" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-7" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Final Notes&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) nominal damages can support punitive damages for&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;(2) intentional trespass&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(3) because society values the right to exclude regardless of physical or economic harm&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(4) &amp;nbsp;only awarding nominal damages would incentivize &lt;b&gt;&quot;self-help&quot; building walls, guns, to keep others out, and society wants to avoid that. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="400" x="420" y="-850" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-13" edge="1" parent="1" source="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-9" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-12" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-9" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Claude question&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- True or false: Under the ad coelum doctrine as interpreted by the court in Hinman v. Pacific Air Transport, a landowner owns the airspace above their property to an unlimited height, and therefore any flight over private land — regardless of altitude — constitutes an actionable trespass. Briefly explain.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="270" x="940" y="-150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-15" edge="1" parent="1" source="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-12" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-14" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-12" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;my answer&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- False. the modern version of Ad Coelum limits the ownership of airspace to real economic or physical harms, with clean hands and not malice, &amp;nbsp;the judicial justification for this is that it would create endless litigation if all flights had hundreds of cases of trespass as they flew above homes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="270" x="1010" y="-380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-14" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;my answer&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;In Hinman,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) &amp;nbsp; rejected a literal reading of the ad coelum doctrine,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2) &amp;nbsp;a landowner owns only as much airspace as they &lt;b&gt;use and occupy &lt;/b&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(3) &lt;b&gt;Overflight is not a trespass unless&lt;/b&gt; it causes &lt;b&gt;actual and substantial interference with that use&lt;/b&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;JJ: &lt;b&gt;applying ad coelum literally&lt;/b&gt; would &lt;b&gt;open the door to endless litigation &lt;/b&gt;any time a plane crossed over private property, an outcome both &lt;b&gt;impractical&lt;/b&gt; and contrary to the doctrine&#39;s original purpose.&quot;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="370" x="990" y="-690" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="L1b-FcRtrCj5sE13cWqp-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-16" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="L1b-FcRtrCj5sE13cWqp-1" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D2Jrq7Rm3lbFnPPIpjT8-16" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Question&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Owen owns a plot of land in a rural area and wants to drill a water well near the boundary of his property. His neighbor Paula wants to install a septic system in the same area, but state health regulations prohibit a septic system from being located within a certain distance of a water well. Only one of the two systems can be installed in that location. Paula argues that Owen&#39;s well constitutes a private nuisance because it prevents her from installing her septic system. Applying the rule from Hendricks v. Stalnaker, assess the merits of Paula&#39;s claim.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="420" x="1730" y="-150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-OxtAIcw0qxLtMy-bzP-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="L1b-FcRtrCj5sE13cWqp-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="p-OxtAIcw0qxLtMy-bzP-1" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="L1b-FcRtrCj5sE13cWqp-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;My Answer&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Using Hendricks, Paula would likely fail because the court has to weight the social benefit of the water well against Paula&#39;s septic tank, and the benefits here are equal so because the water well was there first the septic tank is blocked. This would change if the water well was placed only to block the septic tank , even if malicious it would have to not benefit the other party. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="420" x="1620" y="-350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-OxtAIcw0qxLtMy-bzP-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-align: center; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Final&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Using Hendricks,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;(1) The court balances the social utility of the competing uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;(2) both are necessary,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;value roughly equal - claim fails&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;Result might differ:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;(3) &lt;/span&gt;installed the well purely out of spite with no legitimate benefit to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;himself, as that could tip the unreasonableness finding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="420" x="1680" y="-560" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
