        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="uIjVV1aGW-ahsy_Uf4_k-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;independent covenants&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Paradine v. Jane&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;independent covenants&lt;/b&gt; means the landlord cannot evict for non-payment without a separate contractual provision allowing it&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Smith exception:&amp;nbsp;IS dependent on the landlord&#39;s not breaching the covenant of quiet enjoyment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="10565" y="2080" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="uIjVV1aGW-ahsy_Uf4_k-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Constructive Eviction&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Blackett v. Olanoff&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;A (1) &lt;b&gt;substantial deprivation&lt;/b&gt; of the tenant&#39;s quiet enjoyment for a (2) &lt;b&gt;substantial period of time&lt;/b&gt;, (3) &lt;b&gt;traceable to the landlord&lt;/b&gt;, that makes the property unfit for the purpose for which it was leased.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="11305" y="2300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="uIjVV1aGW-ahsy_Uf4_k-5" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Repudiation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Surrender&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Gotlieb v. Taco Bell Corp.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;An express statement rejecting surrender does NOT override conduct that constitutes acceptance. Courts look at actual conduct, not stated intent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Mere attempt to re-let ≠ acceptance, must be more. like here where written proposal&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="10950" y="2630" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="uIjVV1aGW-ahsy_Uf4_k-8" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Dependent Covenants&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Medico-Dental Co. of LA v. Horton &amp;amp; Converse&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;A tenant&#39;s obligation to&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;pay rent is dependent on the landlord&#39;s compliance with a covenant in the lease if that covenant goes to the root of the consideration&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="11030" y="2100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="uIjVV1aGW-ahsy_Uf4_k-11" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;Implied Warranty of Habitability&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Javins v. First National Realty Corp.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;an implied warranty of habitability — &lt;/b&gt;the landlord must maintain the premises in compliance with the housing code throughout the lease term.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Noise is not a housing code violation&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="10360" y="2280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="uIjVV1aGW-ahsy_Uf4_k-14" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Duty to Mitigate&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Sommer v. Kridel&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;a residential tenant surrenders a lease&lt;b&gt;,&lt;/b&gt; the landlord has a duty to mitigate damages by making a reasonable effort to re-let the premises.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="340" x="10400" y="2510" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-11" edge="1" parent="1" source="KX1l3vwAFacsqiBSdOgY-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-10" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="KX1l3vwAFacsqiBSdOgY-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Covenants Running with the Land&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Mullendore Theatres v. Growth Realty Investors&lt;/i&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;text-decoration-line: underline;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) A covenant runs with the land only if it touches and concerns the land.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;promise to pay money that places no restriction on how that money is used does not touch and concern the land&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="10840" y="3820" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="KX1l3vwAFacsqiBSdOgY-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;Assignment / Restraints on Alienation&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Kendall v. Ernest Pestana&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Assignment: Prime tenant transfers the entire remaining interest in the lease&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Sublease: Prime tenant transfers an interest that terminates before the prime lease&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;a (1) &lt;b&gt;commercial landlord&lt;/b&gt; may NOT (2) unrea&lt;b&gt;sonably withhold consent to an assignment&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="350" x="11240" y="3990" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="KX1l3vwAFacsqiBSdOgY-6" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;Equitable Lien / Mechanic&#39;s Lien&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Timmer v. Gray&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mechanic&#39;s Lien&lt;/b&gt; gives a repairer rights against the property they worked on:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;[1] Continued possession of the item by the lienholder&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;[2] Filing with the relevant state authority&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Equitable Lien, based on unjust enrichment to prevent an inequitable windfall:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Lien works against anyone BUT a GFPV&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="380" x="11300" y="4250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="KX1l3vwAFacsqiBSdOgY-9" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Foreclosure&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Murphy v. Financial Development Corp.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;A mortgagee (1) conducting a foreclosure sale owes the mortgagor duties of (2) good faith and due diligence — essentially fiduciary duties — (3) in its role as seller at the foreclosure auction.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Good faith&lt;/b&gt; = play fair; no purposeful disregard of duty or intentional harm to the mortgagor&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Due diligence&lt;/b&gt; = try hard; act as a reasonable person would in voluntarily selling their own home&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="380" x="10140" y="3930" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="KX1l3vwAFacsqiBSdOgY-12" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Forfeiture vs. Foreclosure&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Skendzel v. Marshall&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) under an installment land contract defaults, the appropriate remedy is (2) judicial foreclosure, not forfeiture — (3) even if the contract expressly provides for forfeiture.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Narrow Exception for forfeiture&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Buyer abandoned the property&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2) Buyer has paid only a small portion of the purchase price (minimal equity at stake)&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="360" x="10420" y="3730" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-3" edge="1" parent="1" source="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-2" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-6" edge="1" parent="1" source="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-4">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ixjWyndOjYlyef1FcQsJ-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="ixjWyndOjYlyef1FcQsJ-1" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#3399FF);" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Gifts&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="8970" y="4170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;Inter Vivos Gifts /&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Delivery Requirement&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Irons v. Smallpiece&lt;/i&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;text-decoration-line: underline;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;For a valid inter vivos gift of personal property, there must be:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Donative intent — present intent to make an irrevocable gift now&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2) Delivery — either of a deed of gift OR actual delivery of the thing itself&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(3) Acceptance by the donee&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="400" x="9040" y="3920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8y4niLV66Yt3knxzj_6Q-4" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Gift Causa Mortis&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Foster v. Reiss&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Core Rule: A gift causa mortis requires &lt;b&gt;actual delivery&lt;/b&gt; of the gifted item. A note telling the donee where to find something&lt;b&gt; is not delivery&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Three Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Made when the donor believes death is imminent (contemplation of death)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2) Delivery — same strict standard as inter vivos gifts&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(3) Gift is automatically rescinded if the donor survives&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="440" x="9390" y="4120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ixjWyndOjYlyef1FcQsJ-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Deed Delivery&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Gilbert v. McSpadden&lt;/i&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;text-decoration-line: underline;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;For a deed to effectively transfer real property&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2)&amp;nbsp;grantor intended the deed to be presently operative and effective&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Thus:&amp;nbsp;Intent to deliver ≠ delivery. Strictly enforced.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;*Grantee&#39;s ignorance doesn&#39;t automatically defeat delivery&amp;nbsp;presume acceptance&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="400" x="8920" y="4420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#3399FF);" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Landlord-Tenant Law&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Lease Types&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;(2)&amp;nbsp;Possession&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;(3) Conditions/Warranties: Quiet Enjoyment,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;Constructive Eviction, and the Implied Warranty of Habitability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(4)&amp;nbsp;Lease Transfers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(5) Privity&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(6)&amp;nbsp;Tenant Breach&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="10830" y="2350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-2" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-6" edge="1" parent="1" source="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-2" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-5" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-9" edge="1" parent="1" source="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-2" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-7">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-11" edge="1" parent="1" source="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-2" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-10" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fnYyX7579Ygv_hZD4wmJ-1" edge="1" parent="1" source="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-2" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-12">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="y_eXBYPTVWxm5DhW20qM-5" edge="1" parent="1" source="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-2" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="y_eXBYPTVWxm5DhW20qM-3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=light-dark(#000000,#3399FF);" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Real Estate Transactions and Finance&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Transfer Rules: Nemo Dat&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;(2)&amp;nbsp;Void vs. Voidable Title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;(3) Equitable Conversion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(4)&amp;nbsp;Security Interests: Mortgages&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(5) Recording Acts: Race, Notice, and Race-Notice&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="12340" y="2250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Equitable&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;title&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Wood v. Donohue&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Upon execution of a (1) land sale contract (including an installment contract), (2) equitable title immediately vests in the buyer. (3)&amp;nbsp;seller retains only legal title as security for purchase price.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Benefits that accrue to the property → buyer&#39;s&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Risk of loss → buyer&#39;s&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="12325" y="2540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-5" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Nemo Dat&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;(void title)&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Kunstsammlungen zu Weimar v. Elicofon&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&quot;Nemo dat quod non habet&quot; — one cannot give what one does not have.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;theft = void title doesn&#39;t matter GFPV&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="320" x="11920" y="2190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-7" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Voidable Title / Not GFPV&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Kotis v. Nowlin Jewelry&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Voidable Title — what creates it:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Nowlin knew he was transferring title to the Rolex&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Good Faith — the test:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the buyer&#39;s actual belief, not reasonable person&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="320" x="12710" y="2535" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-10" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Fraud in the Execution&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Fraud in the execution: A is misled about what he is giving up — doesn&#39;t even realize he&#39;s signing away property rights → VOID title&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Exception: If A was negligent in allowing himself to be defrauded, A may be estopped from asserting void title against a GFPV.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="11920" y="2460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="y_eXBYPTVWxm5DhW20qM-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-12" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="y_eXBYPTVWxm5DhW20qM-1" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1fwdeR0jmVJhn6tfra2_-12" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Recording Acts&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;to provide conditions where a later purchaser can deviate from this baseline and prevail over an earlier one&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;are statutes that allow a subsequent purchaser to &quot;beat&quot; an earlier one, provided they are a Good Faith Purchaser for Value (GFPV)&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="340" x="12420" y="2040" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="y_eXBYPTVWxm5DhW20qM-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Race-Notice statute&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Core Rule: Under a race-notice recording act, a later purchaser defeats an earlier unrecorded interest only if they purchased:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Without notice of the prior interest, AND&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2) For valuable consideration and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(3) records first&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;Here,$1 was not enough to be valuable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;The burden of proof falls on the party claiming GFPV status&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="370" x="12660" y="1790" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="y_eXBYPTVWxm5DhW20qM-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Adverse Possession vs. GFPV&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Mugaas v. Smith&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;A mature adverse possession claim is binding upon a bona fide purchaser for value even when:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="330" x="12820" y="2170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qI1jlyZk0DCSy2Svmtut-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Easement by Necessity&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Schwab v. Timmons&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Elements:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Common ownership of dominant and servient tracts prior to severance&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2) One of the severed parcels is otherwise landlocked at the moment common ownership was severed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Here: can&#39;t sell land then demand easement by necessity, create your own problem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="380" x="11200" y="4570" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="XRqVtVAv-GfinTpq3Xuv-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Prescriptive Easement&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Warsaw v. Chicago Metallic Ceilings, Inc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Elements: OCASD&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Open and notorious — use visible to the property owner&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Continuous — uninterrupted for the statutory period&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Adverse/nonpermissive — without the owner&#39;s permission&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Statutory period — varies by jurisdiction (5 years in State of Charney)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Definite and certain line of travel — slight deviations okay; substantial changes defeat it&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(Actual use) — sometimes listed separately&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Mere Acquiescence ≠ Permission&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;JJ&lt;/b&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Majority: Prescriptive easements reduce litigation and protect long-term use&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="380" x="10435" y="4860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;Easement by Estoppel&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Warsaw v. Chicago Metallic Ceilings, Inc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;When a landowner (1) grants a license and the licensee, (2) relying on that permission, (3) materially changes position at considerable expense, (4) the license becomes irrevocable&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Three Elements (from the slides):&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;License — owner&#39;s permission for another to use property&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Reliance — user materially changes position in reliance on the license&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Harm — user would be harmed if license were revoked&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;irrevocable&lt;/b&gt; for &quot;as long as the nature of the license calls for.&quot;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="400" x="10770" y="4540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-4" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;Negative Easements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Warsaw v. Chicago Metallic Ceilings, Inc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Core Rule: There is no legal right to the free flow of light and air from a neighboring property.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Even a structure with some malicious motive is not enjoin-able if it serves a useful and beneficial purpose.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;A structure erected solely out of spite with no useful purpose = spite fence → can be enjoined&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="400" x="10290" y="4590" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-7" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Scope of Easement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Penn Bowling v. Hot Shoppes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Rule 1: An easement appurtenant cannot be used to benefit land other than the dominant estate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Rule 2: Misuse of an easement does NOT constitute forfeiture, waiver, or abandonment of the easement. Overuse stops the use, not the easement itself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Ways to terminate an easement:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Deed from easement holder to servient estate owner extinguishing the easement (release)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Merger — dominant and servient tracts come under common ownership&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Adverse possession of the servient estate (if AP extinguishes the easement)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Abandonment — easement holder manifests intent never to use it again (mere non-use ≠ abandonment; must be affirmative act showing intent to abandon)&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="485" x="10080" y="4270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-14" edge="1" parent="1" source="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-10" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-13" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-10" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Covenants Running with the Land&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Tulk v. Moxhay&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) A party who purchases property with knowledge of a restrictive covenant burdening the land must honor the covenant. Where a covenant was intended to run and touches and concerns the land,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Equitable Servitude Burden Runs When:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Intent — parties intended the covenant to bind successors&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Touch and concern — the covenant is substantively connected to the land&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Notice — the party against whom enforcement is sought had notice (actual, constructive, or inquiry)&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="360" x="11040" y="3500" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-16" edge="1" parent="1" source="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-13" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-15" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-13" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Covenants Running with the Land&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Neponsit Property Owners&#39; Association v. Emigrant Industrial Savings Bank&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Three Requirements for Real Covenant to Run (from the case):&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Intent — grantor and grantee intended covenant to run with the land&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Touch and concern — the covenant substantially affects ownership rights in the property&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Privity of estate — between the party claiming benefit and the burdened party&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="360" x="11520" y="3410" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdfIAW2kgq_moO4frY10-15" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Touch and Concern&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Eagle Enterprises v. Gross&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Core Rule: A covenant touches and concerns the land only if it substantially affects the property owner&#39;s legal interest in the property itself. Simply saying &quot;this covenant runs with the land&quot; in the deed is not enough&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="360" x="11970" y="3340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
