        <mxCell id="_CKNJFoMzXsLgvQAXU5i-8" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;In Gross&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) Gives someone the right to use another&#39;s land, but unlike an appurtenant easement, it (2) doesn&#39;t benefit any particular parcel of land — it (3) benefits a person or entity directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;English courts don&#39;t like these cuz wild unclaimed part of deeds, American does like &#39;commercial&#39;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="390" x="300" y="1160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
